  "body": "Part of #2574 (research answer 7).\n\nMaintainer request, 2026-11-18, in his words (quoted in #2574):\n> \"Alot of the basis is already there but it is it's own executable. That could be launched from within camcraft\"\n\n## Scope\n- `xtask/src/release_pack.rs` line 54: add `camcraft-sim` to `EXES`, and update `xtask/src/release_tests.rs`.\n- `.github/workflows/release.yml`: add `-p camcraft-simview` to the build lines (Linux line 54, macOS lines 105-106, Windows line 195), to the sign step (line 214), and to the package content checks (tar, deb, rpm, AppImage, snap, flatpak, macOS zip and dmg).\n- macOS: put the binary in `CamCraft.app/Contents/MacOS` beside `camcraft-ui`.\n- Linux: the binary sits beside `camcraft-ui` in each package (the launch of #2589 finds it there).\n- No new workflow trigger.\n- A change in `.github/` waits for the maintainer at review (`needs-maintainer`).\n\n## Done means\nA release build of the three platforms contains `camcraft-sim` beside `camcraft-ui`, and the package checks of `release.yml` and the xtask release tests assert it.\n\nDepends on #2586.\n",
